+## Symlinks
+
+Symbolic links stored in an archive are skipped unless `-l/--links` is
+in use. With `--links` each symlink is listed under its name plus a
+`.rclonelink` suffix, its size is the length of the link target and
+reading it returns the target. This is the same representation the
+[local backend](/local/#symlinks-junction-points) uses, so copying an
+archive with `--links` recreates its symlinks on a destination which
+supports them.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A regular archive member whose name happens to end in `.rclonelink`
+is still read as a regular file.
+
 ## Hashes
 
 Which hash is supported depends on the archive type. Zip files use
